     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day, which is twice the labeled maximum for metformin. The maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release and 2,000 mg/day for extended-release. A dose this high greatly raises the risk of lactic acidosis, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nWhich of these did you mean?\n\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals.** This is 2,550 mg/day, the usual maximum.\n- **1000 mg PO twice daily with meals.** This is 2,000 mg/day.\n- **1700 mg total per day.** For example, 850 mg PO twice daily with meals.\n- **Another dose.** If 1700 mg three times daily is what you want, tell me and I'll enter it with a note that you confirmed the dose.\n\nOnce you confirm, I'll enter the order right away."
      }
     ],
